{
  "requirement": "Each bundled skill MUST open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. Each bundled skill, recognized by its front matter, is a site:\n\n:::{sites} skills\n```yaml\nlanguage: markdown\npaths: [assets/skills]\nrule:\n  kind: minus_metadata\nmatch:\n  - \"---\\nname: example\\n---\\n\\n# Example\\n\"\nno_match:\n  - \"# Example\\n\"\n```\n:::",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** Each bundled skill MUST open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. Each skill is a site, so each site reviews its own file. The one obligation the test also covers is the shared structural check.\n\n**Site query.** `skills` uses `kind: minus_metadata` over `assets/skills` in Markdown. It selected exactly five files:\n- `assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md`\n- `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`\n- `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md`\n- `assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md`\n- `assets/skills/habeas-refactor/SKILL.md`\n\nA search for files in `assets/skills` that start with `---` found the same five and no others. The `references/*.md` files carry no front matter, so the query correctly leaves them out. The test's `SKILLS` constant lists the same five names, so the query neither misses a skill nor selects anything outside the requirement's scope.\n\n**Query snippets.** The match snippet is front matter followed by a heading. The no_match snippet is the same heading with no front matter. Together they show what the rule keys on, which is front matter, so they are adequate.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_open_with_their_workflow_as_ordered_steps]` loops over every skill in `SKILLS` and checks these obligations:\n- *Opens with the workflow, before any other section.* The first `## ` heading in the raw `SKILL.md` must equal `## Workflow`. The assertion is `assert_eq!` and names the skill.\n- *Ordered steps.* `workflow_steps` parses the numbered `- [ ] N.` items in the Workflow section. The test requires at least two steps. It also requires the numbers to equal `1..=n` exactly, which rules out missing, duplicated, or out-of-order numbering.\n\nA skill whose first section was not Workflow, or whose steps were unnumbered or misordered, would fail these assertions. I found no unchecked obligation and no gap in the site query.",
  "references": "bdd2c44e881310eaa176cac0bc633689971a0bf7aef8b3b2d4d14ac7fe919877",
